Oculus Community Port for Forge — Minecraft 26.3 module
=====================================================

Target: Minecraft 26.3 / Forge 66.1.2 / Java 25, OpenGL client.
This is an unofficial community port, not an official Oculus, Iris, Forge,
Sodium, Embeddium, Mojang or Microsoft release or endorsement.

The community port is distributed under LGPL-3.0-only. See
LICENSE-oculus-forge.txt (LGPLv3), the accompanying LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt (GPLv3),
and LICENSE_NOTES.md for provenance and corresponding-source build context.
The included GPL text does not change this project's LGPL-3.0-only designation.

The complete 26.3 source build uses versions/26.3 and the shared root src/, build
wrapper, authored test inputs and third-party notices. A sources JAR alone is
not the complete build tree. The 0.4.0-beta.4 source target is the separate branch
https://github.com/Khaliiid0/Oculus-Community-Port/tree/release/26.3-0.4.0-beta.4
See versions/26.3/SOURCE_BUILD.md there. Verify the corresponding revision before
distributing a public binary; a local source ZIP alone is not public availability.

JCPP 1.4.14, Copyright Shevek, is bundled under Apache License 2.0 and relocated
to dev.oculusforge.bundle.jcpp. See META-INF/licenses/JCPP-LICENSE.txt.
External shader packs, Minecraft game binaries and developer/runtime fixtures
are not included in the mod binary.

Minecraft and Mojang are trademarks of Microsoft Corporation. OptiFine and other
shader renderers are incompatible with this port. This module does not claim
Fabric, NeoForge, every shader option, or complete Iris rendering parity.

The shader-prism icon is original AI-assisted community-port branding, not the
original Oculus/Iris logo and not a gameplay screenshot.
